    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-ēlĕgans</span></b> ,
			antis, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very neat</i>, <i>fine</i>,
			or <i>elegant</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 67, 270</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Planc. 24, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					1, 7, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-ēlĕganter</span></b> ,
				<i>very finely</i>, <i>very
			elegantly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pereleganter dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 52, 197</span></i>
			.</div>
